 "interpretation": {
  "observed_fact": "Every learning-method file is byte-identical to the G2 launch manifest; 86/86 evaluator and 131/131 setup tests pass; the oracle passes on this run's seed; 30/30 coverage rows are complete. Three seeds completed 64 updates (320 optimizer steps, 64 EMA updates each) with zero integrity events and twelve complete finite 4,096-sample arrays. The raw actor's held-out utility rose in every seed: -1.1436 -> +4.6249, -0.5994 -> +4.7675, -0.6146 -> +4.5347 (z -0.135 -> +0.834, -0.043 -> +0.858, -0.046 -> +0.819); per-seed paired intervals [+5.545, +5.988], [+5.140, +5.601], [+4.926, +5.375]; pooled paired delta +5.4282 with 95% [+5.2985, +5.5585] on 12,288 pairs. Gap closure 10.6479%, 10.0073%, 9.5987%; the median 10.0073% clears the frozen 10% threshold by 0.0073% of the gap, and seed 3 alone sits below it. The EMA telemetry closed 0.099%, 0.119%, 0.195% (pooled 95% [+0.0116, +0.1386]; every per-seed interval includes zero) and moved 0.9-2.0% of the raw displacement. The landscape, first-period outcomes and all four endpoints of every seed replay bitwise; eleven artifacts bind one source commit.",
  "supported_inference": "Using the parity-correct setup-learning method, the raw generation actor reliably learns an independently generated synthetic setup landscape within 64 setup updates from outcome-only feedback: the improvement is present in every seed with paired intervals far from zero, and the frozen practical-margin criterion on the median gap closure is met. The G2 raw-actor finding therefore replicates on a fresh table with fresh seeds, and the frozen rule returns PROCEED for the synthetic trainability portion of G2. The EMA telemetry repeats the G2 pattern: at the paper's 0.999 decay updated once per setup update (0.999^64 = 0.937975 retained, ~1,000-update time constant) it lags severely behind the raw actor within this budget; this is recorded, not decided upon.",
  "plausible_but_untested": "The gap-closure fraction is landscape-dependent: on this table the raw actor gained about half the utility it gained on the G2 table in the same 64 updates, from a higher initial utility toward a lower optimum, so the 10% fraction is met narrowly here and comfortably in G2. A fourth table from the same family could fall on either side of the threshold under the same strength of learning; the learning signal itself (pooled lower bound about 0.9 uniform SD above zero) is not in doubt. A longer budget would very likely close more of the gap (the raw curves are still rising at update 64) and would eventually carry the EMA.",
  "claim_not_supported": "That the method learns Stratego setups (no game was played; the landscape is synthetic). That the EMA at this budget is a usable evaluation model (its pooled telemetry interval barely excludes zero and every per-seed interval includes it). That the 10% gap-closure threshold is cleared robustly: the median exceeds it by 0.007 percentage points of the gap. Any authorization of G3, a Stratego game experiment or Phase 8 warmstart training."
 },
