 "g2_gate": "PROCEED for the synthetic trainability portion of G2: the parity-correct raw learner reliably learns a fresh landscape within 64 updates under the frozen criteria; the practical-margin criterion is met at its edge",
 "why_not_stop": "STOP is reserved for a parity-correct raw learner that fails the frozen criteria; every criterion is met.",
 "why_not_revise": "no implementation or measurement defect exists: parity, replay, binding and integrity all pass, and an unfavourable result was not observed; the thin threshold margin is a property of the frozen criterion on this landscape draw, not a defect.",
 "scope_of_this_decision": "closes only the synthetic trainability portion of G2 and authorizes designing the next gate; it does not authorize launching G3, any Stratego game experiment, or the full Phase 8 warmstart.",
 "recommended_next_question": {
  "text": "Before any Stratego-facing setup training: what evaluation model and update budget give Gate G3 an instrument with power? Specifically, does a design in which the setup learner trains on real outcomes against the frozen Phase 8 teacher schedule, is evaluated on a paired setup-development pack under the amended evaluation rule identity (O-P18-EVALRULES-1), and reads the EMA only after a budget commensurate with its ~1,000-update time constant (or a predeclared, reviewed alternative evaluation model for the pilot) improve over its fresh initialization by a predeclared margin whose sampling variability is known?",
  "gate": "G3 design (setup-only Stratego benefit), first half: improvement over the fresh initialization",
  "why_it_discriminates": "The two synthetic runs establish that the raw learner learns; what they do not establish is a Stratego-facing evaluation design that can see it. Two constraints are now measured: the EMA needs a budget on the scale of a thousand setup updates (or a different evaluation model for a pilot), and a practical margin defined as a fraction of a landscape-dependent gap can sit at its own edge; the next gate's margin should be sized from a known instrument resolution in the units the gate is scored in. The evaluation contract's rule identity must be amended before any real-game measurement.",
  "explicitly_not_started": "No G3 run, no Stratego setup-learning game, no Phase 8 warmstart training, no tuning, no push."
 },
